# The e2e suite reads fixture notes back and asserts on their bytes — the tasks journey compares a
# ticked line against a whole-line literal — so a Windows runner checking these out with CRLF turns
# a passing tick into a "\r"-only diff. Pinned to LF here rather than normalized in the assertion:
# the product splits on "\n" on both the read and the write side, so the "\r" round-trips correctly
# and the fixture, not the expectation, is what has to be the same bytes everywhere. Scoped to the
# fixtures whose contents tests read.
e2e-tests/fixtures/**/*.md text eol=lf
# manual-variables.test.ts compares this page's CSS fences with these snippets byte for byte.
docs/user/reference/css-variables.md text eol=lf
e2e-tests/fixtures/e2e-docs-css-variables/.obsidian/snippets/*.css text eol=lf
e2e-tests/fixtures/e2e-appearance-snippets/.obsidian/snippets/one-view.css text eol=lf
